Z||000000||Ted||06-19-99||09:19 AM||||<br>I'm a new member and I got my Fiero a couple of weeks ago.  I was wondering how to make my Fiero faster without putting a new engine in it. I don't know a whole lot about cars but I know you guys do. I have an '85 2m4. Thanks in advance
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||06-19-99||09:44 AM||||Hi Ted, and welcome to the club. There are a whole bunch of things you can do to improve performance. Some have more effect than others and it really all kind of depends on how much money you are willing to spend.
Z||000002||batboy||06-19-99||10:37 AM||||The easiest and best way to increase flow and power (and even add better fuel economy) is to install a good set of headers and a good flowing exhaust system. Improving the exhaust system significantly increases both torque and horsepower. It is probably the best bang for your buck and often overlooked. The best part is that you don't have to pull the engine to do it.<p>If you have the 2.5 liter, 4 cylinder, you are extremely limited in the high performance department. Don't get me wrong, I think the "iron duke" is a great engine, it just wasn't meant to be hotrodded. If you desire more power, you should of gotten a V6 car. Don't despair, the 4 banger Fieros are still fun to drive, I have one myself, and they get great gas mileage. Do what I did. Use that one during the week as a daily driver, then save up and get a hotrod Fiero for the weekends. Good luck.
